From 78df83646c53ff5bb8ff52e3401c2930e0db64b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:06:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] libview: Give the view's scroll controller its axes

The GtkEventControllerScroll of EvView had no flags. In GTK 4 a scroll
controller without axes never emits scroll, so ev_view_scroll_event()
never ran and Ctrl+wheel no longer zoomed; the scrolled window still
scrolled, which hid the problem.

The handler returns FALSE for what it does not handle, so the scrolled
window keeps scrolling as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libview/evince-view.ui | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libview/evince-view.ui b/libview/evince-view.ui
index 899aec4..2563c29 100644
--- a/libview/evince-view.ui
+++ b/libview/evince-view.ui
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@
     </child>
     <child>
       <object class="GtkEventControllerScroll">
+        <!-- Without axes the controller never emits scroll; Ctrl+wheel zooms -->
+        <property name="flags">both-axes</property>
         <signal name="scroll" handler="ev_view_scroll_event" />
       </object>
     </child>
-- 
